module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Cech.GenPairCechPresheaf
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Cech.RingIdealSite

/-!
# Forgetting the chosen family: the generated pairs over the rings with an ideal

A generated pair `(A, f_1, …, f_r)` has an ideal, `(f_1, …, f_r)`, and a morphism of generated
pairs carries that ideal onto the ideal of its target
(`Stacks.GenPairSite.GenPair.Hom.map_ideal`). So there is a functor
`Stacks.RingIdealSite.forgetElts` from the generated pairs `Stacks.GenPairSite.GenPair r` to the
rings with an ideal `Stacks.RingIdealSite.RingIdeal`, forgetting the chosen family.

The complex of presheaves of modules `K^•` on these two categories is **one complex**: the one on
generated pairs is the pullback along `forgetElts` of the one on rings with an ideal, degreewise
and with the same differential and augmentation. This is the precise sense of "`K` depends only
on the ring and the ideal, not on the chosen family" — the value of `K` is a colimit over the
finite sets of generating families of the ideal, and the chosen family enters it nowhere.

Why it matters for [Stacks, Tag 099E]: that proof needs the complexes attached to two finitely
generated ideals `I, I' ⊆ ℐ(U)` of possibly different numbers of generators, and on generated
pairs those live on the two unrelated categories `GenPair r` and `GenPair s`. Through the
identifications of this file both are pullbacks of the single presheaf on rings with an ideal,
along the two functors of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.ringIdealFunctor`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.ringIdealFunctor_comp_eq` compares them.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.RingIdealSite.forgetElts` — the functor forgetting the chosen family of a generated
  pair.
* `Stacks.RingIdealSite.pullbackGenPair` — the pullback of presheaves of modules along it.

## Main results

* `Stacks.RingIdealSite.pullbackGenPair_kTerm`,
  `Stacks.RingIdealSite.pullbackGenPair_kDiff`,
  `Stacks.RingIdealSite.pullbackGenPair_kComplexNat`,
  `Stacks.RingIdealSite.pullbackGenPair_kAugZero` — **the complex of
  `Stacks.GenPairSite.kComplexNat` and its augmentation are the pullback along `forgetElts` of
  `Stacks.RingIdealSite.kComplexNat` and `Stacks.RingIdealSite.kAugZero`.**

## Implementation notes

The identifications are all `rfl`: both constructions descend the same cocones out of the same
filtered diagram `Stacks.GenSetCech.cechDiagram A I`, indexed by the ring and the ideal alone, and
the structure presheaf of rings of the generated pairs is the pullback of the structure presheaf
of rings of the rings with an ideal on the nose.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached: this is a comparison of two models of one construction.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099E)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.RingIdealSite

open Stacks.GenPairSite

variable {r : ℕ}

/-- **Forgetting the chosen family of a generated pair.** The ideal it generates is carried onto
the ideal by every morphism of generated pairs, which is what a morphism of rings with an ideal
asks for. -/
def forgetElts (r : ℕ) : GenPair.{u} r ⥤ RingIdeal.{u} where
  obj P := { ring := P.ring, commRing := P.commRing, ideal := Stacks.GenPairSite.ideal P }
  map u := { toRingHom := u.toRingHom, map_ideal := GenPair.Hom.map_ideal u }
  map_id _ := RingIdeal.Hom.ext' rfl
  map_comp _ _ := RingIdeal.Hom.ext' rfl

/-- The ring underlying the image of a generated pair under `forgetElts` is its ring. -/
@[simp]
theorem forgetElts_obj_ring (P : GenPair.{u} r) : ((forgetElts r).obj P).ring = P.ring := rfl

/-- The ideal of the image of a generated pair under `forgetElts` is the ideal generated by its
chosen family. -/
@[simp]
theorem forgetElts_obj_ideal (P : GenPair.{u} r) :
    ((forgetElts r).obj P).ideal = Stacks.GenPairSite.ideal P := rfl

/-- The ring homomorphism underlying the image of a morphism of generated pairs under `forgetElts`
is its ring homomorphism. -/
@[simp]
theorem forgetElts_map_toRingHom {P Q : GenPair.{u} r} (u : P ⟶ Q) :
    ((forgetElts r).map u).toRingHom = u.toRingHom := rfl

/-- **The pullback of presheaves of modules along `Stacks.RingIdealSite.forgetElts`.** -/
abbrev pullbackGenPair (r : ℕ) : RingIdealModule.{u} ⥤ GenPairModule.{u} r :=
  PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀ (forgetElts.{u} r).op structureRings.{u}

/-- **The degree-`n` term of the complex on generated pairs is the pullback of the degree-`n`
term of the complex on rings with an ideal.** -/
theorem pullbackGenPair_kTerm (n : ℕ) :
    (pullbackGenPair.{u} r).obj (kTerm.{u} n) = Stacks.GenPairSite.kTerm.{u} (r := r) n := rfl

/-- **The differential of the complex on generated pairs is the pullback of the differential of
the complex on rings with an ideal.** -/
theorem pullbackGenPair_kDiff (n : ℕ) :
    (pullbackGenPair.{u} r).map (kDiff.{u} n) = Stacks.GenPairSite.kDiff.{u} (r := r) n := rfl

/-- **The augmentation of the complex on generated pairs is the pullback of the augmentation of
the complex on rings with an ideal.** -/
theorem pullbackGenPair_kAugZero :
    (pullbackGenPair.{u} r).map kAugZero.{u} = Stacks.GenPairSite.kAugZero.{u} r := rfl

/-- Restriction of presheaves of modules along `Stacks.RingIdealSite.forgetElts` preserves zero
morphisms, a morphism being carried to the morphism with the same components. -/
instance preservesZeroMorphisms_pullbackGenPair :
    (pullbackGenPair.{u} r).PreservesZeroMorphisms where
  map_zero _ _ := PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun _ ↦ rfl

/-- **The complex of presheaves of modules on the generated pairs is the pullback along
`Stacks.RingIdealSite.forgetElts` of the complex on the rings with an ideal.** -/
theorem pullbackGenPair_kComplexNat :
    ((pullbackGenPair.{u} r).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℕ)).obj kComplexNat.{u} =
      Stacks.GenPairSite.kComplexNat.{u} r := by
  refine HomologicalComplex.ext rfl ?_
  rintro i j rfl
  exact congrArg (fun w ↦ (pullbackGenPair.{u} r).map w) (kComplexNat_d.{u} i)
    |>.trans ((pullbackGenPair_kDiff.{u} (r := r) i).trans
      (Stacks.GenPairSite.kComplexNat_d.{u} (r := r) i).symm)

end Stacks.RingIdealSite

end
